Circuit: R1 (1kΩ) goes from +9V to node M; from M to GND there are two parallel branches:
• Branch A: R2 (2kΩ);
• Branch B: R3 (1kΩ) and R4 (1kΩ) in series, with the node between them called X.

Calculation:
1. Branch B = 1k + 1k = 2kΩ;
2. The two branches in parallel = 2k ∥ 2k = 1kΩ;
3. Voltage at M = 9 × 1k / (1k + 1k) = 4.5V;
4. X is between R3 and R4, so its voltage = 4.5 / 2 = 2.25V.

The tests measure the voltages at M and X relative to GND.
